# split-4x6: split board with 4 rows by 6 columns per half and 3 thumb keys per half (Corne-like, with a number row).
# Columns are staggered (middle finger highest, pinky lowest), the halves are 2.5 units apart, the thumb keys sit one
# row below the letters. Stagger values are approximate; edit the y values to match a real board. One unit = 19.05 mm.
# Not on this board: = [ ] \ the function row and the arrow keys (they sit on layers on such boards); shortcuts
# that use them are skipped on import.
name split-4x6
pitch 19.05

key ` 0 0.5 1
key 1 1 0.5 1
key 2 2 0.25 1
key 3 3 0 1
key 4 4 0.25 1
key 5 5 0.35 1
key 6 8.5 0.35 1
key 7 9.5 0.25 1
key 8 10.5 0 1
key 9 11.5 0.25 1
key 0 12.5 0.5 1
key bksp 13.5 0.5 1
key tab 0 1.5 1
key q 1 1.5 1
key w 2 1.25 1
key e 3 1 1
key r 4 1.25 1
key t 5 1.35 1
key y 8.5 1.35 1
key u 9.5 1.25 1
key i 10.5 1 1
key o 11.5 1.25 1
key p 12.5 1.5 1
key - 13.5 1.5 1
key esc 0 2.5 1
key a 1 2.5 1
key s 2 2.25 1
key d 3 2 1
key f 4 2.25 1
key g 5 2.35 1
key h 8.5 2.35 1
key j 9.5 2.25 1
key k 10.5 2 1
key l 11.5 2.25 1
key ; 12.5 2.5 1
key ' 13.5 2.5 1
key lshift 0 3.5 1
key z 1 3.5 1
key x 2 3.25 1
key c 3 3 1
key v 4 3.25 1
key b 5 3.35 1
key n 8.5 3.35 1
key m 9.5 3.25 1
key , 10.5 3 1
key . 11.5 3.25 1
key / 12.5 3.5 1
key rshift 13.5 3.5 1
key lsuper 3 4.45 1
key lalt 4 4.45 1
key lctrl 5 4.45 1
key space 8.5 4.45 1
key enter 9.5 4.45 1
key ralt 10.5 4.45 1

finger LP ` 1 tab q esc a lshift z
finger LR 2 w s x
finger LM 3 e d c
finger LI 4 5 r t f g v b
finger LT lsuper lalt lctrl
finger RT space enter ralt
finger RI 6 7 y u h j n m
finger RM 8 i k ,
finger RR 9 o l .
finger RP 0 bksp p - ; ' / rshift

home LP a
home LR s
home LM d
home LI f
home LT lalt
home RT enter
home RI j
home RM k
home RR l
home RP ;

mod ctrl lctrl
mod alt lalt ralt
mod super lsuper
mod shift lshift rshift
